\section{Writing your own}{

A bound term is the value of \code{\link[=gddm_bound_term]{gddm_bound_term()}}. Its \code{fn} is called on
the tape as \code{fn(t, p, ctl)} for a plain number \code{t}, and returns a list
with \code{B}, the boundary at that time, and \code{dlogB}, its logarithmic
derivative \verb{B'(t) / B(t)}. The solver needs the second because the
change of variable that pins the walls contributes a \verb{-y B'(t)/B(t)}
term to the drift; supplying it rather than differencing \code{B} keeps the
rescaled drift exact.
